am-ui lossless route: answer Apple's credential request once per kind and sign-in.

Upstream answers every credential request with the same Apple ID and password. When Apple refuses
them and its library asks again, the same wrong password is sent a second time, and each refusal
counts toward Apple's account lockout; a repeated code request appends a second code to the first.
With this patch a repeated request of either kind ends the sign-in ("... requested again, aborting
login") and the person starts a new attempt with corrected input. Applies on top of 0001-0003.
Sign-in mode only (the service runs without credentials and is unchanged).

--- a/lite/auth.cpp
+++ b/lite/auth.cpp
@@ -56,6 +56,22 @@
              std_string_data(_ZNK17storeservicescore18CredentialsRequest7messageEv(credReqPtr->obj)),
              need2FA ? "true" : "false");
 
+    /* am-ui: one password answer and one code answer per sign-in. A repeated
+       request means Apple refused the previous answer; answering again with
+       the same values would only count toward Apple's account lockout (and a
+       second code would be appended to the first one). Sign-in mode only:
+       the service has no credentials to repeat. */
+    if (amPassword) {
+        static int password_answers = 0;
+        static int code_answers = 0;
+        int* const answers = need2FA ? &code_answers : &password_answers;
+        if (++*answers > 1) {
+            LOG_WARN("%s requested again, aborting login",
+                     need2FA ? "verification code" : "credentials");
+            _exit(1);  /* like the other exits of the sign-in child */
+        }
+    }
+
     int passLen = amPassword ? (int)strlen(amPassword) : 0;
 
     if (need2FA) {
